  "details": "I've suggested this on Discord but it wasn't seen by le important people and it got minimal attention so I asked and decided to post it here.\n\npsst, this is Feature Request number #200, yay\n-------\n\nI have a suggestion for Discord:\n Adding a role self-give command to @VRCBot, region roles.   [Example: !role Europe]\nSince we're having our discord filled with more new users, it would be nice to have a way of giving ourselves a general region role, this will make it easier to identify who's from what region and also may even help on tagging for different region events like \"@Europe peeps, meet up at 10min!\" of course the commands could only be used in #bottalk and you may only have 1 region role, attempting to do the command again with another region would overwrite the current one.\n\nRegions could be:\n- North America\n- South America\n- Europe\n- Africa\n- Asia\n- Australia/Oceania\n(maybe less, maybe more?)\n\nAlso in some way they need to be listed somewhere so users know what region roles they can have. (and \"!rolelist\" command to check what's available)\nTheir role permissions can be the same as \"VRChatter\" and are below the VRChatter role on the role list. (Only who has \"VRChatter\" can do the command ofc)\nTheir color can somewhat correspond to the region/continent but they can all just have the same color.",
